From: Wiam Khader <Wiam@wiamox.com>
Subject: [PATCH] uname: report WiamOX as the operating system (uname -o)

Replaces the earlier edit of gnulib's m4/host-os.m4 (linux* -> 'WiamOX'),
which a release tarball ignores (configure is already generated) and
"git submodule update" throws away. Same result: uname -o prints WiamOX,
uname -s comes from the WiamOX kernel (linux/patches/).

Made against coreutils v9.12-74-g9c7cf20c3 (git).
---
--- a/src/uname.c
+++ b/src/uname.c
@@ -48,6 +48,12 @@
 #include "quote.h"
 #include "uname.h"
 
+/* WiamOX: uname -o names the distribution.  Set here rather than in
+   gnulib's m4/host-os.m4, so it works the same for a release tarball and
+   a git clone and survives "git submodule update".  */
+#undef HOST_OPERATING_SYSTEM
+#define HOST_OPERATING_SYSTEM "WiamOX"
+
 /* The official name of this program (e.g., no 'g' prefix).  */
 #define PROGRAM_NAME (uname_mode == UNAME_UNAME ? "uname" : "arch")
 
